  pages = {1--17},
  abstract = {In this paper a distinction is made between subjective competence and objective competence. Several constructs have been introduced in the literature to refer to the individual's knowledge, beliefs and feelings about his competence. An overview of the most important constructs is given. A heuristic model of the affective learning process is presented and used as a framework for describing appraisal processes. The nature of a specific form of appraisal, viz. self-assessment, is outlined. It is argued that self-assessment should be a major component of any competence category and that it is a key variable in independent learning.},
