cation, 11 (3), pp. 317-334. , doi:10.1080/13603110701238769; Gregoriou, Z., Commencing the rhizome: Towards a minor philosophy of education (2004) Educational Philosophy and Theory, 36 (3), pp. 233-251. , doi:10.1111/j.1469-5812.2004.00065.x; Grosz, E., A thousand tiny sexes: Feminism and rhizomatics (1994) Gilles Deleuze and the theater of philosophy, pp. 187-210. , In: Boundas C. V., Olkowski D., editors New York, New York,: Routledge; Honan, E., (Im)plausibilities: A rhizo-textual analysis of policy texts and teachers' work (2004) Educational Philosophy and Theory, 36 (3), pp. 267-281. , doi:10.1111/j.1469-5812.2004.00067.x; Honan, E., Writing a rhizome: An (im)plausible methodology (2007) International Journal of Qualitative Studies in Education, 20 (5), pp. 531-546. , doi:10.1080/09518390600923735; Jove, G., How do I improve what I am doing as a teacher, teacher educator and action-researcher through reflection? A learning walk from Lleida to Winchester and back again (2011) Educational Action Research, 19 (3), pp. 261-278. , doi:10.1080/09650792.2011.600526; Kamberelis, G., The rhizome and the pack: Liminal literacy formations with political teeth (2004) Spatializing literacy research and practice, pp. 161-197. , In: Leander K. M., Sheehy M., editors New York, New York,: Peter Lang; Lather, P., Drawing the line at angels: Working the ruins of feminist ethnography (1997) International Journal of Qualitative Studies in Education, 10 (3), pp. 285-304. , doi:10.1080/095183997237124; Le Grange, L., The 'theoretical foundations' of community service-learning: From taproots to rhizomes (2007) Education as Change, 11 (3), pp. 3-13. , doi:10.1080/16823200709487174; McInnis, C., James, R., McNaught, C., (1995) First year on campus: Diversity in the initial experiences of Australian undergraduates, , Canberra, Canberra,: Australian Government Publishing Service; O'Riley, P.A., (2003) Technology, culture, and socioeconomics, , New York, New York,: Peter Lang; Scott, J.D., Grellier, J., Wild minds searching: Early scholars groping in the gap (2012) disClosure: A Journal of Social Theory, 21. , http://www.as.uky.edu/socialtheory, Self/Story, 54-70. Retrieved from; Sellers, W., Gough, N., Sharing outside thinking: Thinking (differently) with Deleuze in educational philosophy and curriculum inquiry (2010) International Journal of Qualitative Studies in Education, 23 (5), pp. 589-614. , doi:10.1080/09518398.2010.500631; St Pierre, E.A., An introduction to figurations: A postcultural practice of inquiry (1997) Qualitative Studies in Education, 10 (3), pp. 279-284. , doi:10.1080/095183997237115; St Pierre, E.A., Methodology in the fold and the irruption of transgressive data (1997) International Journal of Qualitative Studies in Education, 10 (2), pp. 175-189. , doi:10.1080/095183997237278; Stronach, I., The space is not yet blank: Anthropologies for a future action research (2002) Educational Action Research, 10 (2), pp. 291-308. , doi:10.1080/09650790200200186; Tuan, Y.F., (1997) Space and place: The perspective of experience, , Minneapolis, Minneapolis,: University of Minnesota Press},
  abstract = {Philosopher Gilles Deleuze and psychoanalyst F\'elix Guattari's figuration of the rhizome describes structures that are non-hierarchical and open-ended. Rhizomatic analyses are increasingly being adopted in educational research to challenge traditional power structures, give voice to those previously unheard and open issues in messy but authentic ways. Rhizomatic mapping involves depicting a number of points that elaborate, shape and disrupt each other, encouraging readers to draw their own interconnecting routes or separating chasms between them. In this paper, I adopt rhizomatic mapping techniques to open up issues of learning spaces in one Australian university, in order to problematise the mass university's approaches to student learning. In this mapping, I give voice to two of the least powerful groups in the university, first-year students and sessional tutors, alongside educational academics and administrators. \copyright{} 2013 Copyright HERDSA.},
  langid = {english},
  keywords = {/unread,ethnography,first-year experience,qualitative research,reflective practice,student experience}
}

