  abstract = {The procedure of ego-state reframing is described, and its application to an academic setting illustrated by reference to three cases. One of these is a lecturer who used the technique to overcome his anxiety before large classes; a second is a tutor able to become closer to her students; and a third employed the technique to overcome a writing block. The efficacy of the approach is discussed in terms of the four elements essential to successful psychotherapy. \copyright{} 1985, Taylor \& Francis Group, LLC. All rights reserved.},
