y, M., (2004) The student assessment handbook: New directions in traditional and online assessment, , Abingdon, UK, Abingdon,: RoutledgeFalmer; O'Donovan, B., Price, M., Rust, C., Know what I mean? Enhancing student understanding of assessment standards and criteria (2004) Teaching in Higher Education, 9 (3), pp. 325-335. , doi:10.1080/1356251042000216642; O'Donovan, B., Price, M., Rust, C., Developing student understanding of assessment standards: A nested hierarchy of approaches (2008) Teaching in Higher Education, 13 (2), pp. 205-217. , doi:10.1080/13562510801923344; Price, M., Assessment standards: The role of communities of practice and the scholarship of assessment (2005) Assessment & Evaluation in Higher Education, 30 (3), pp. 215-230. , doi:10.1080/02602930500063793; Price, M., Carroll, J., O'Donovan, B., Rust, C., If I was going there I wouldn't start from here: A critical commentary on current assessment practice (2010) Assessment & Evaluation in Higher Education, , (iFirst); Ramsden, P., (1992) Learning to teach in higher education, , London, London,: Routledge; Rowntree, D., (1987) Assessing students: How shall we know them?, , London, London,: Kogan Page; Rust, C., Price, M., O'Donovan, B., Improving students' learning by developing their understanding of assessment criteria and processes (2003) Assessment & Evaluation in Higher Education, 28 (2), pp. 147-164. , doi:10.1080/02602930301671; Sadler, R., Ah!... So that's quality (2002) Assessment: Case studies, experience and practice from higher education, pp. 130-136. , In: Schwartz P., Webb G., editors London, London,: Kogan Page; Sadler, R., Transforming holistic assessment and grading into a vehicle for complex learning (2009) Assessment, learning and judgement in higher education, pp. 45-63. , In: Joughin G., editors Dordrecht, Dordrecht,: Springer Science+Business Media BV; Scott, G., (2005) Accessing the student voice: Using CEQuery to identify what retains students and promotes engagement in productive learning in Australian higher education, , http://www.dest.gov.au/sectors/higher_education/publications_resources/profiles/access_student_voice.htm, Canberra, Canberra,: DEST, Retrieved October 25, 2010, from; Stevens, D.D., Levi, A.J., (2004) Introduction to rubrics: An assessment tool to save grading time, convey effective feedback and promote student learning, , Sterling, VA, Sterling, VA,: Stylus; Taylor, J., Assessment in first year university: A model to manage transition (2008) Journal of University Teaching & Learning Practice, 5 (1), p. 3; Thomson, R., Curtis, G., An institutional approach to standards-based assessment: Evaluating early-stage implementation, , Poster presented at the ATN Assessment Conference, November 2009, Melbourne, Melbourne,: RMIT; Toohey, S., (1999) Designing courses for higher education, , Buckingham, UK, Buckingham,: Society for Research in Higher Education & Open University Press; (2007) Trends in student satisfaction at UWS 2004-2006, , http://www.uws.edu.au/opq/planning_and_quality#4, University of Western Sydney (UWS), Retrieved September 17, 2010, from; (2009) Assessment policy: Criteria and standards-based assessment, , http://policies.uws.edu.au/view.current.php?id=00227, UWS, Retrieved September 17, 2010, from; (2009) Unit outline and learning guides policy, , http://policies.uws.edu.au/view.current.php?id=00154, UWS, Retrieved September 17, 2010, from; Yorke, M., Formative assessment in higher education: Moves towards theory and the enhancement of pedagogic practice (2003) Higher Education, 45 (4), pp. 477-501. , doi:10.1023/A:1023967026413},
  abstract = {Assessment expectations are communicated to students in various ways and at different points in the semester. The provision of written information in learning guides given to students at the start of semester articulates what they are to do and how well they are to perform in assessment tasks. This paper examines how assessment expectations at an Australian university were communicated by staff in 159 first-year units (subjects) in the first year of university-wide implementation of criteria and standards-based assessment and learning guides policies. A framework was developed to analyse the extent and types of assessment information provided in learning guides. The paper provides a snapshot of the types of assessment used in the first year, including exams and analytical, reflective and authentic tasks. The paper contributes to an understanding of how university-wide assessment policy implementation can be evaluated through an examination of documents produced by staff. \copyright{} 2013 Copyright HERDSA.},
  langid = {english},
  keywords = {/unread,assessment expectations,evaluation of policy implementation,first year,standards-based assessment,types of assessment}
}

